log.txt
git-ignore
*#
debug*
release*
clang*
paper*
# Whitelist the small, paper-tracked summary tier under paper-data/<tag>/.
# Raw per-run CSVs (paper-data/<tag>/raw/) stay ignored — they are large
# (3+ GiB per cell) and reproducible from the binaries via the runner.
# See PAPER_SWEEP.md §Output format.
!paper-data/
!paper-data/*/
!paper-data/*/summary/
!paper-data/*/summary/*
!paper-data/*/manifest.yaml
# Operational log of the runner — large and not paper material.
paper-data/*/run.log
paper-data/*/sweep.out
paper-data/*/sweep.err
paper-data/*/sweep.pid
# Raw per-run CSV+log tree — large (~3 GiB/cell), reproducible from
# binaries via the runner. The earlier paper-data/ un-ignore chain
# made these visible to `git status`; this re-ignores them silently.
paper-data/*/raw/
*.err
*.out
*.csv
# Re-allow summary CSVs after the broad *.csv ignore above.
!paper-data/*/summary/*.csv
/size/
/.vscode/
stderr.txt
*.mk
perf*
!**/PERFORMANCE.md
!**/perf_context_capture.hpp
leanstore.json
.claude
/TRASH
*.pdf
/test_data*
/test_csv*
test*.json
/test*data
/test*csv
*.bak